  "title": "India's coal energy crisis intensifies as power plants face critical storage issues",
  "summary": "India's coal power plants are experiencing a significant energy crisis, with nearly 40% of plants operating at a critically low fuel level. The situation has led to a sharp increase in the number of power plants with only less than 25% of the required inventory or generating power for less than three days, as reported by the Central Electricity Authority.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Nearly 40% of India’s coal power plants are running critically low on fuel.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The number of power plants with only less than 25% of the required inventory or less than three days of power rose sharply to 74.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "India’s Central Electricity Authority reported coal inventories at thermal power stations fell to 22.9 MT on September 19.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
